// std::types — fundamental Holt types (types skill §1-2, §16-18).
//
// These types are provided by the standard library and distributed with the
// compiler. They are automatically available to every Holt source file —
// no import is required:
//
//   int age = 25
//   string name = "John"
//   bool active = true
//   i32 count = 42
//   u8 flags = 255
//
// Full list: bool, string,
//   i8 i16 i32 i64 i128 int,
//   u8 u16 u32 u64 u128 uint,
//   float double.
//
// `int`/`uint` are pointer-sized (i64 width on 64-bit).
// The compiler has intrinsic knowledge of their representations
// (see llvm_int_for_bits in compiler/src/codegen/mod.rs) but they are
// architecturally standard-library types, not compiler keywords:
// sized names lex as Ident and resolve via Ty::from_stdlib_name
// (compiler/src/sema/mod.rs) with no import needed.
//
// This module intentionally declares nothing: importing it is a no-op.
// It exists so the implicit environment has a canonical home.
